# Thinkway Enterprise Platform Architecture v1.0 (Frozen)

**Milestone:** `docs/architecture/THINKWAY_ENTERPRISE_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_V1.md`  
**BPN foundation:** `docs/architecture/BUSINESS_PROCESS_NAVIGATION_FOUNDATION.md`  
**Campaign Workspace OS (canonical):** `docs/architecture/CAMPAIGN_WORKSPACE_BASELINE_V1.2.md` — Lifecycle OS / Decision Center / Operational Readiness; **Maintenance Mode**; no redesign without Architecture Reopen  
**Historical:** `docs/architecture/CAMPAIGN_WORKSPACE_BASELINE_V1.1.md` · `docs/architecture/CAMPAIGN_WORKSPACE_BASELINE_V1.md`  
**Compliance template:** `docs/architecture/PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE_COMPLIANCE.md`  
**Package:** `docs/architecture/platform-ux/` (docs 01–12 frozen)

## Product definition

Thinkway is a **campaign-centric enterprise operating system**. The campaign is the single business object; the campaign lifecycle is the single business process. Stakeholder journeys enter that lifecycle at different stages. Nothing may exist outside this model.

## Canonical navigation

**Business Process Navigation** is the approved navigation foundation. The Campaign Workspace Lifecycle OS extends BPN (State Strip, Process Rail, Decision Center, Next Action). Future modules integrate into the Campaign Lifecycle — they do not introduce new pages, parallel workflows, competing guidance panels, or separate-application experiences.

## Frozen — do not redefine

- Navigation philosophy (Platform → Module → Business Process Navigation → Content)
- Workspace philosophy / Campaign Lifecycle Architecture (doc 12)
- Stakeholder Journey Architecture (doc 11)
- Enterprise UX standards / Financial Display Standard
- Campaign Module Baseline + BPN Foundation + **Campaign Workspace Baseline v1.2**

**No architectural redesign** unless Product formally reopens Architecture v1.0.  
**No new architecture docs or UX redesign initiatives** unless Architecture Reopen is approved.

## Campaign Workspace v1.2 — mandatory preserve

Future Campaign Workspace changes **must** satisfy:

1. Preserve **Business Stage SSOT**  
2. Preserve **Decision Center** (only operational guidance component — extend, do not replace)  
3. Preserve **Lifecycle OS**  
4. Preserve **Next Action Journey** (executable, stage-specific, exact-record CTAs)  
5. Preserve **Progressive Disclosure** (Lifecycle Details **and** collapsed operational registers)  
6. Preserve **Workspace-as-View** philosophy  

Also preserve: shared lifecycle object · Hard Block ≠ Needs Attention · object-specific blockers · KPI-only workspace banners · deep-link matrix.

**Do not redesign Campaign Workspace without Architecture Reopen approval.**  
**Do not perform further Campaign Workspace UX refinement** — Maintenance Mode only.

**Maintenance Mode only:** bug fixes · performance · accessibility · copy · additional deep-links · lifecycle extensions that preserve the baseline.

**Regression (protected):** `npm run test:campaign-workspace-lifecycle-os`.

## Operational effort gate

No capability may be implemented until its specification answers how it reduces operational effort: tasks **eliminated**, **simplified**, and remaining **human decisions**.

## Mandatory for every ADR / capability spec / release architecture / implementation proposal

Include section **Platform Architecture Compliance** covering:

1. Campaign Lifecycle stage(s) extended (S00–S18 from doc 12)  
2. Stakeholder Journey(s) extended  
3. Business Process component(s) reused (`lib/business-process`, Decision Center, process rail, state strip, process-aware tabs, etc.)  
4. Why no new navigation philosophy is introduced  
5. Workspace(s) extended · baselines referenced (incl. Campaign Workspace v1.2) · no duplicate workflow · lifecycle extension paragraph  
6. Operational effort reduction (eliminated / simplified / human)  
7. Campaign Workspace invariants preserved when touching Campaign surfaces  

## Implementation posture

- Architecture-first work is **complete**. Prefer **capability specifications** then functional delivery.  
- Extend BPN + Campaign Workspace Baseline **v1.2**; do not reinvent them.  
- **Active initiative:** Release 2.3 — Campaign Planning Workspace — start with Business Capability Review → Product UX Review → Capability Spec approval → Architecture Compliance → Implementation. **No Campaign Workspace UX work.**  
- Planning Workspace = Planning stage of Campaign Lifecycle; must inherit Campaign Workspace Lifecycle OS v1.2 (Decision Center; progressive registers; no new nav/layouts/workflows/competing guidance).  
- After 2.3: Media Plan Copilot → Client/Vendor/Creator journeys → Reporting → Notifications → Analytics.
